WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.010
Like it or not, the holidays will inevitably
end — and life will crash back into its

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.840
normal routines, with all its jobs and stress
and winter chores.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.580
"Always winterize your pipes."

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.200
So relax a little and enjoy some of Netflix's
newest releases.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.220
January sees the addition of some incredible
new programming to ring in the New Year.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.980
Here's what's in store for January 2018, starting
with the Netflix originals.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.260
Glacé: Season 1

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.320
If you liked the French show Les Revenants,
you're bound to fall in love with Netflix's

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.160
newest French offering, Glacé.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.680
Also known as The Frozen Dead in English,
Glacé is set high in an isolated mountain

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:43.110
range, where a police officer stumbles across
a small-town mystery that's been kept in the

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:43.820
dark for years.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.500
Look for it January 1st.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.760
Lovesick: Season 3

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.460
Considering that this show's original release
title was Scrotal Recall, you can get a pretty

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.520
clear idea of what kind of humor to expect.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.940
The story starts when Dylan finds out he has
an STD and decides to visit every girl he's

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.240
been with to warn them about it.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.500
"How've you been."

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.600
"I have chlamydia"

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.220
"Terrific!"

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:10.600
The show originally aired on the UK's Channel
4 in 2014, and Netflix began airing it as

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.180
an original with the second season.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.400
Check out Season 3 of Lovesick when it drops
on January 1st.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.500
Before I Wake

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.840
Directed by Mike Flanagan, Before I Wake is
about a couple's newly adopted son who has

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.280
the uncontrolled ability to manifest his dreams
in the real world.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.860
Haunted by real-life nightmares, the couple—played
by Kate Bosworth and Tom Jane—have to figure

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.360
out why their little orphan boy is inadvertently
unleashing his night terrors on the world.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.579
Before I Wake was filmed in 2013, but the
release date was continually pushed back until

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.800
the movie was dropped from Relativity's release
schedule altogether.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.380
Netflix acquired the film's international
rights in 2017 and proceeded to release the

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.660
film everywhere except in the United States,
but the wait is finally over.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:58.420
Before I Wake will hit U.S. Netflix on January
5th...five years after it was made.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.360
Comedians in Cars Getting Coffee

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.520
Jerry Seinfeld's Emmy-award winning web series
has been running since 2012, and it's making

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.980
the move to Netflix as part of Seinfeld's
massive, jillion-dollar deal with the streaming

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:10.480
service.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:16.100
Rebranded as a Netflix original, the series
is about...well, exactly what it says on the

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.580
box: comedians hang out in a car, getting
coffee.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.100
Then, they talk about things, and it's hilarious.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.250
If somehow you've missed this show over the
years, you'll be able to catch up on every

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:30.960
episode on January 5, along with 24 brand
new episodes available only on Netflix.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.660
DEVILMAN crybaby: Season 1

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:39.620
An adaptation of one of the most violent,
gratuitous mangas of the '70s, Devilman: Crybaby

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:43.360
is easily one of the most hotly anticipated
anime releases of the new year.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.080
The story centers on a boy who merges with
a demon to become Devilman in the hopes of

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.080
stopping Hell from taking over the Earth.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.280
In their review of the first three episodes,
Anime-Now basically described the show as

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.900
a mature version of the Looney Tunes.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.220
Buckle in for the ride on January 5th.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Rotten

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.280
This six-part documentary series dives into
the global food industry to take a look at

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.540
modern farming practices and the impact they're
having on the world.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.490
Rotten promises to dig into corruption in
agricultural businesses, food additives, and

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.360
all the other hot button food issues.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.840
Whether it hits or misses, there's one thing
you can count on: a ton of terrible Rotten

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.020
Tomatoes puns once the reviews start rolling
in.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.200
Check it out for yourself on January 5th.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.100
Alejandro Riaño Especial de stand up

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.700
The first new comedy special to hit Netflix
in the new year is Alejandro Riaño Especial

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.480
de stand up, which will see the Colombian
comedian taking the stage to deliver his unique

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.160
brand of rapid-fire jokes.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.740
Take a look on January 6th.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.100
Disjointed: Part 2

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:49.040
The first season of Kathy Bates' stoner comedy
Disjointed wasn't exactly a smoking success,

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.520
at least where critics were concerned.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:56.640
The story centers on Ruth Feldman, a Los Angeles
dispensary owner with a team of vaguely competent

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.580
"budtenders," one of whom is her own son.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:03.600
The first ten episodes were released August
25th, and Netflix is set to roll out the rest

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.100
of the season on January 12, 2018.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.480
Somebody Feed Phil

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.440
No, this isn't a resurgence of Viva la Bam.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:16.240
Somebody Feed Phil is a travel and cooking
show following Phil Rosenthal, the creator

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:20.509
of Everybody Loves Raymond and self-proclaimed
foodie, as he travels around the world tasting

00:04:20.509 --> 00:04:22.880
the best cuisine the planet has to offer.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.360
Rosenthal is no stranger to culinary travels
— he previously starred in the similar series

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.460
I'll Have What Phil's Having, which is also
available on Netflix.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.240
Check out Somebody Feed Phil on January 12th.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.040
The Polka King

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:41.100
Based on the real life story of Jan Lewan,
a polka personality who concocted a Ponzi

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:46.629
scheme that stole somewhere in the neighborhood
of $10 million, The Polka King is a new Netflix

00:04:46.629 --> 00:04:48.400
original film starring Jack Black.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:53.740
The feature film draws from the 2009 documentary
The Man Who Would Be Polka King, which is

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.960
also arriving on Netflix on January 12th.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.560
You can't stop the polka.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.980
Tom Segura: Disgraceful

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:05.479
Veteran stand-up comic and podcaster Tom Segura
is arriving with an all-new special on January

00:05:05.479 --> 00:05:08.789
12th, marking his third full-length special
on Netflix.

00:05:08.789 --> 00:05:13.490
If it's anything like Segura's other stand-up,
Disgraceful will be full of his sharp wit,

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:16.120
low-key delivery, and completely irreverent
topics.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:17.700
Find out on January 12.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.240
Katt Williams: Great America

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.880
Comic legend Katt Williams has been making
audiences laugh since well before he became

00:05:24.889 --> 00:05:26.560
a household name in 1999.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.080
In 2018, he's still going strong.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:32.780
His newest special, Great America, arrives
on January 16.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.220
Tiempos de guerra: Season 1

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:41.560
Translating to Times of War, Tiempos de guerra
is an upcoming scripted Spanish series set

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.000
during the Spain-Morocco War of 1921.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.840
The show show follows the nurses and doctors
of a hospital tasked with treating wounded

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.909
soldiers, so get ready for lots of historical
drama.

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:54.000
You can start watching on January 18th.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.260
Grace and Frankie: Season 4

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.340
Over three seasons, viewers have been delighted
by the escapades of Grace and Frankie, which

00:06:01.349 --> 00:06:05.250
follows two women who find out that their
husbands have been having an affair for the

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.060
past 20 years...with each other.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.780
"Saul and I are in love."

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:09.780
"Excuse me?"

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:10.790
"You're gay?"

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:12.060
"We want to get married."

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:12.560
"Oh…"

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:13.220
"Married!?"

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.220
"Because we can do that now"

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:15.000
"I know!

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.480
I hosted the fundraiser."

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.699
Lily Tomlin and Jane Fonda star as the leading
ladies, with Sam Waterston and Charlie Sheen

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:22.960
as their ex-husbands.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.080
Queue up Season 4 on January 19th.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.000
The Open House

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:33.120
Not to be confused with the 2010 bomb Open
House or the 1987 cult horror B-movie of the

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:38.229
same name, The Open House is a 2018 horror
film about a mother and son who move into

00:06:38.229 --> 00:06:41.820
a new house — only to find their lives threatened
by mysterious forces.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:47.260
The Open House sees yet another Netflix collaboration
with actor Dylan Minnette, who also starred

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.540
in 13 Reasons Why.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.640
The Open House, well, opens on January 19th.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.700
Todd Glass: Act Happy

00:06:54.389 --> 00:06:58.479
Todd Glass entered the national consciousness
with his appearances on NBC's reality show

00:06:58.479 --> 00:07:02.650
Last Comic Standing, and he's since gone on
to make a name for himself as one of the funniest

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:03.560
comedians in the business.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.160
Look for his newest special, Act Happy, on
January 23.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.560
Ricardo Quevedo: Hay gente así

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:15.990
Netflix has been loading up on foreign acquisitions
lately, and 2018 will see a wave of new multilingual

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:21.009
comedians like Ricardo Quevado, a Colombian
native who was featured on Comedy Central's

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:22.180
Stand-Up Without Borders.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.880
Now, he's hitting Netflix with Hay gente así.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.440
Check it out on January 24.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.640
A Futile and Stupid Gesture

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.990
National Lampoon gave us such comedy gems
as Animal House and Vacation, along with more

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.480
questionable gems like, uh, everything else
they made.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:43.800
"Get ready for… Van Wilder: Freshman year."

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:48.100
But there's no doubt the magazine and its
films have made a lasting mark on popular

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:48.600
culture.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:53.860
That's the angle of A Futile and Stupid Gesture,
a film about the early days of the national

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.120
sensation and its eventual downfall.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:57.780
Check it out on January 26.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:07:59.760
Dirty Money

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:05.520
Along with their food exposé Rotten, Netflix
is also releasing a documentary investigation

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.280
into the world's largest corporations.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:13.020
Created by Alex Gibney, who won an Oscar for
his documentary Taxi to the Dark Side, Dirty

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:17.560
Money will be an episodic series with multiple
documentarians taking the helm for different

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.060
episodes.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.940
Take a look on January 26th.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.640
One Day at a Time: Season 2

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:28.460
Loosely based on the series of the same name
that first aired in 1975, One Day at a Time

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:32.830
follows a family with three generations living
under the same roof as they try to make their

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:33.440
lives work.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:38.480
Following solid reviews for the first season,
released in 2017, Netflix announced plans

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.550
to release a second season in 2018.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:43.520
All 13 new episodes drop on January 26.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:46.440
Babylon Berlin: Seasons 1 &amp; 2

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:51.620
Set in the 1920s, this German-language drama
follows a police commissioner who's transferred

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.860
to Berlin to investigate the Russian mafia.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:59.320
Touted as the most expensive German show ever
produced, Babylon Berlin enjoyed strong ratings

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:03.720
in Germany, and Netflix secured the US distribution
rights well before the first episode aired.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.500
Both seasons will drop on Netflix on January
30.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.800
That covers all the Netflix originals.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.540
Now let's take a look at everything else arriving
on Netflix in January 2018.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:14.360
New movies

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:19.740
Oscar season arrives early on Netflix, with
multiple award-winners and nominees slated

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.430
to land on the service in January 2018.

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:26.690
On the first of the month, look out for dramas
such as The Godfather trilogy, The Shawshank

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:28.840
Redemption, Midnight in Paris, and Training
Day.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:32.680
"King Kong ain't got s--- on me."

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:37.700
On the action front, the first of the year
also sees the addition of most of the Batman

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:42.640
films, starting with 1989's Batman all the
way to 2005's Batman Begins.

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:44.900
Yup, even Batman &amp; Robin.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.540
"If I must suffer, humanity will suffer with
me."

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:54.480
Plus, go ahead and let that holiday spirit
linger a little longer with the second best

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:59.410
Christmas movie written by Shane Black — Lethal
Weapon and all its sequels land on January

00:09:59.410 --> 00:09:59.910
1st.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.660
In the same spirit, Christmas may be over,
but there's never a bad time of year to experience

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.100
the ups and downs of Richard Curtis' modern
classic Love Actually.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:13.760
That arrives on Netflix on January 1st, along
with other comedies like Wedding Crashers,

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.000
Caddyshack, and the Bring It On pentology.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:17.900
Yeah, they made five of those.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:23.220
If you're making it a resolution to watch
more documentaries in 2018, Netflix as you

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.220
covered there too.

00:10:24.509 --> 00:10:29.700
The first of the month sees the addition of
2017 documentaries like AlphaGo, Maddman:

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:33.540
The Steve Madden Story, and Martin Luther:
The Idea that Changed the World.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.300
Netflix's kids' line-up is geared toward the
whole family this January.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.980
"The suspense is terrible.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:39.490
I hope it'll last."

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:45.720
New Year's Day heralds the addition of the
1971 classic Willy Wonka &amp; the Chocolate Factory,

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:50.720
along with 2007's Stardust, based on the Neil
Gaiman novel of the same name.

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:55.200
And on the 31st, Disney/Pixar's Cars 3 will
be available for streaming.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:59.860
Finally, the weather won't be the only thing
giving you chills this January.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:04.310
Netflix is adding a handful of thrillers to
their service as 2018 rolls through the door,

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:09.240
including 30 Days of Night, The Exorcism of
Emily Rose, and Peter Jackson's slow-burning

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.360
The Lovely Bones on the first of the month.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:17.420
As January continues, you can look forward
to The Conjuring on the 8th and the 2017 shark-fest

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.140
47 Meters Down on the 10th.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.140
New television

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:26.579
While most of Netflix's new television offerings
in January will be Netflix originals, you'll

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.000
still be able to find new seasons of some
shows.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:34.680
Highlights include Season 3 of Eastsiders
on the 1st, all five seasons of Episodes on

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:37.460
January 6th, and Season 2 of Colony on the
12th.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:43.180
Also, keep an eye out for the 2018 Olympic
Winter Games Preview on January 15, and Season

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.920
4 of Friday Night Tykes on the 17th.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:50.540
Finally, January 28th heralds the arrival
of The Ministry of Time, a Spanish language

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.000
time-travel adventure series.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:56.340
No matter what you're in the mood to watch
this January, you're bound to find something.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:57.540
Thanks for watching!

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.140
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.520
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

